{
  "key": "pr-1783",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "build-mobile: pass GH_TOKEN=RELEASE_PAT to the release create step (fatal: bad repository '')",
    "description": "## Problem

The mobile leg's `Create or update GitHub Release` step exported only `GITHUB_TOKEN`; `scripts/release_attach_or_create.sh` builds its tag-push URL from `GH_TOKEN` (`${GH_TOKEN:+https://x-access-token:…}`), so when the tag is missing the push gets an empty remote and dies with `fatal: bad repository ''` (run 39766453580, v1.0.626 — 2026-10-22, after the iOS IPA itself built and signed fine).

## Fix

Mirror what build-macos.yml already does (4 call sites): `GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.RELEASE_PAT }}` on the step env — PAT deliberately, so the tag push fires tag CI (script header comment).

## Notes

- The iOS IPA build + TestFlight submission are unaffected (separate jobs); this only fixes the mobile GitHub release asset/tag creation.
- Verified against the failing run's env block (GITHUB_TOKEN/RELEASE_TAG/VERSION present, GH_TOKEN absent)."
  }
}

